<article class="env-lemma" id="0BPF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BPF">Lemma <span data-tag="0BPF">37.2.6</span>.</a> The property of being a thickening is fpqc local. Similarly for first order thickenings. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The statement means the following: Let $X \to X'$ be a morphism of schemes and let $\{ g_ i : X'_ i \to X'\} $ be an fpqc covering such that the base change $X_ i \to X'_ i$ is a thickening for all $i$. Then $X \to X'$ is a thickening. Since the morphisms $g_ i$ are jointly surjective we conclude that $X \to X'$ is surjective. By Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02L6" data-tag="02L6">35.23.21</a> we conclude that $X \to X'$ is a closed immersion. Thus $X \to X'$ is a thickening. We omit the proof in the case of first order thickenings. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>